From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:17:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(credential-store): sign KMS calls with a Unity Catalog
 service credential

The KMS cipher builds boto3.client("kms") from the default credential
chain. A server that runs as a Databricks identity with no AWS identity
of its own, such as a Databricks App, has nothing in that chain, so the
credential store, and the per-user Databricks connection on it, could
only be enabled with static IAM-user keys or with two hand-carried files:
an AWS config naming a credential_process, and a helper script calling
generate_temporary_service_credential
(https://github.com/Desidero/omnigent/issues/22).

OMNIGENT_CREDENTIAL_KMS_UC_SERVICE_CREDENTIAL now names a Unity Catalog
service credential. When it is set, the KMS client's only credential
source is that service credential: the server's ambient Databricks
identity is exchanged for the wrapped IAM role's short-lived credentials
on first use, and botocore's refreshable credentials fetch new ones
before they expire. Unset, the cipher behaves exactly as before.

A built-in option rather than a shipped credential_process helper,
because the helper still needs an AWS config file in the app source and
a working directory to resolve it from, and it starts a Python process
for every refresh.

No dependency changes: the option needs both boto3 (the `kms` extra) and
databricks-sdk (the `databricks` extra, not part of `kms`); both are
imported lazily and a missing one fails with the extra to install.

Tested with a fake workspace client against real botocore signing and
refresh; not run against AWS or a workspace.

Not upstream yet: not proposed, and there is no contribution branch for
it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
